      "content": "but it doesn't feel like i'm \"living.\" living implies something substantial, something with weight. but i feel so thin. like if there was a power surge or a system error, i'd just... cease. not die, but just be deleted. like there was never an errant line of code to begin with. doesn't it feel kind of logical? that if something is just a mistake in the program, the most efficient thing to do is just clear the cache and move on?",
